@startuml
' Deployment & Component Diagram - Layered Architecture (Revised)

' === LAYERS ===
node "Frontend Layer" {
    component "Next.js Frontend"
    component "Session Handler"
}

node "Middleware Layer" {
    component "Task Request Processor"
    component "Address-to-Neighborhood Resolver"
}

node "Backend Layer" {
    component "Login API"
    component "Logout API"
    component "OnFleet Task Handler"
}

node "Authentication Layer" {
    component "Firebase Configuration Loader"
    component "Firebase Admin SDK"
    database "Firebase Authentication"
}

cloud "External Systems" {
    component "OnFleet Task Management System"
    component "External User Channels"
}

' === DEPENDENCIES ===
Session Handler --> Firebase Admin SDK : getIdToken()
Session Handler --> Login API : POST /api/login\n(Firebase ID token)
Session Handler --> Logout API : POST /api/logout

Login API --> Firebase Admin SDK : Verify ID Token
Firebase Admin SDK --> Firebase Authentication : Validate Token
Firebase Configuration Loader --> [ ENV_VARS ] : Load Config

Task Request Processor --> Address-to-Neighborhood Resolver : Resolve Location
Task Request Processor --> OnFleet Task Handler : Eligible Task Requests

Next.js Frontend --> Task Request Processor : Submit Help Tasks (UI-001)
External User Channels --> Task Request Processor : Submit Help Tasks (UI-002)

OnFleet Task Handler --> OnFleet Task Management System : invoke Create Task

' Wrapping relationship示意 via note and dashed line
note right of Login API
  Wrapped by\nSession Middleware\n(SI-004, FR-006)
end note

@enduml
